BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(PRINCIPAL SEAT, CHENNAI\)
AT CHENNAI

CASE NO: W.P. No. 18920 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: MHC010214892026
DECISION DATE: 2026-03-02
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice D. Krishnakumar & Justice P.B. Balaji

PARTIES:
K. Balasubramanian and 14 others
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
State of Tamil Nadu represented by Principal Secretary, Revenue Department & District Collector, Kancheepuram
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition Act 2013, Constitution of India

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
RFCTLARR Act Section 11, RFCTLARR Act Section 15, Article 226, Article 300A

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
Land Acquisition, Social Impact Assessment, Public Purpose, Natural Justice, Writ of Mandamus

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Petitioners' agricultural lands were acquired for airport expressway expansion without publishing mandatory Social Impact Assessment study report under Section 4 and without hearing objections under Section 15.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Whether compliance with Social Impact Assessment under Chapter II of RFCTLARR Act 2013 is mandatory prior to preliminary notification?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Section 4 of the 2013 Act imposes an inescapable statutory obligation on the government to prepare and evaluate SIA in consultation with local authorities.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Acquisition proceedings initiated without prior Social Impact Assessment study under RFCTLARR Act 2013 suffer from fatal jurisdictional defect and are void ab initio.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Writ Petition Allowed; Acquisition notifications under Act 30 of 2013 quashed for failure to conduct social impact assessment.

Decreed and ord) Tj ET
